WEBVTT

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:12.000
So, uh, today we're gonna walk through the new dashboard feature.
You know, it's, um, basically really cool and super useful for monitoring your application in real time.

00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:18.000
What you'll need first is, uh, you need to have an active account and API access.
That's the, like, the main thing. You also need to know your API key.

00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:25.000
Alright, so, um, first thing you do is you log into the dashboard.
You go to the, you know, the main landing page and click the login button.
Pretty straightforward, like, there's not much to it.

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:32.000
Once you're logged in, you should see the home page. At that point, you're gonna, uh,
you need to navigate to the settings area. That's where you configure everything.

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:39.000
So in settings, you'll see a section called "API Configuration".
Um, you click on that and then you paste your API key.
Make sure it's the right key, you know, the production one, not the test key.

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:45.000
After you paste the key, the system is gonna validate it.
It should say "API Connected" in green. That's when you know it worked, right? That's the validation.

00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:52.000
Okay so now, um, you go back to the home page. You'll see the dashboard is now populated with data.
Like, you can see your application metrics and, uh, like, the health status and stuff.

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:58.000
The dashboard shows you real-time data for your application.
You can monitor memory usage, CPU, request latency, all that good stuff.
